            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous left anterior descending artery to right ventricular fistula.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>467-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a very unusual case of a spontaneously acquired left anterior descending to right ventricular fistula. We believe that this spontaneous occurrence was the result of hemodynamic changes that occurred between the first and second catheterizations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
